  "source": "JoyPro curated on the maker's photo (2026-10-11), F-16EX stick grip alone (no base) seen from behind (pilot side) and slightly from the right: all head controls face the viewer, the front hat sticks out at the right, trigger and the ribbed Rz lever peek out under it",
  "mappingSource": "WinWing \"JOYSTICK GRIP OF F-16 H.O.T.A.S User Manual EN V1.0\" page 4, section 2.1 Button/Functions, EX grip (upper pair of drawings) (https://en.winwing.cn/static/file/JOYSTICK%20GRIP%20OF%20F-16%20H.O.T.A.S-User%20MANUAL%20EN%20V%201.0.pdf): 19 = trim hat, 20 = red round button, 21-25 = cross hat top-left, 26 + Rx/Ry (27-30) = radial ministick below it, 31-35 = knurled rocker, 36-40 = cross hat below the trim hat, 14-18 = hat at the front of the head, 9-13 = hat on the side below the head, 4/5 = trigger, 1/2/41/42/3 + Rz = ribbed lever in front of the trigger, 6 = pinky button, 7/8 + Slider = pinky paddle; matches the catalog numbers",
  "confidence": "high",
  "note": "The Rz lever and its five detent buttons (catalog stick.button.index.1-5 = 1, 2, 41, 42, 3) share one spot on the lever. The catalog note calls it a \"top-rear lever\"; on the manual drawing and the photos it is the ribbed lever under the front of the head, in front of the trigger. Hidden on this view: hat 9-13 (on the grip side near the trigger), pinky button 6 and pinky paddle 7/8 + Slider at the grip base front (gallery-2 shows them). The manual shows no twist on the grip; Z would come from a base. The small gray piece on the left of the grip below the head has no number on the drawing and is not placed. Roll/pitch come from the base; the gimbal marker is at the grip's threaded base joint.",
